        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Cephalaria, Sagina\n- Concepts: flowering plants, plant genera, plant families, native ranges\n\nFacts:\n- Cephalaria is a genus of about 65 species of flowering plants in the family Caprifoliaceae.\n- Cephalaria is native to southern Europe, western and central Asia, and northern and southern Africa.\n- Sagina is a genus of 20–30 species of flowering plants in the family Caryophyllaceae.\n- Sagina and Colobanthus are called pearlworts.",
